---
# A settled report with nothing left to do is where a walk ends, not a
# deadlock.
deadlock_detection: false
---

# Delivering a background child's report to its parent session: from the
# closing entry serve reads (children.go report) through Notify
# (notify.go notifyFrom) to the parent's model, raced against whatever
# the parent's process is doing at that moment. background_agents.fizz
# counts notices at serve; this follows one into the parent.
#
# One child turn, one report, one parent. The report travels:
#
#   closed -> keyed         report saves meta.Reported = the closing seq
#                           BEFORE it notifies (children.go report)
#   keyed -> routed_stdin   notifyFrom saw a lease for the parent. A lease
#                           still starting counts: ch.started() blocks
#                           until its stdin exists, so the write waits for
#                           Mount (the mapped model's "ensure between check
#                           and append" is only the no-lease case below).
#   keyed -> routed_file    notifyFrom saw no lease; the mutex is dropped
#                           before the append (the TOCTOU window)
#   routed_stdin -> in_pipe the {"notice"} line is in the parent's stdin
#                           pipe; serve counts it delivered, nothing is on
#                           disk. A dead child fails the write and falls
#                           through to the append.
#   routed_file -> stored   history.AppendFile, under the file's flock.
#   in_pipe -> waiting      the headless pump read the line and hlNotice
#                           spins (up to 30 s) for job-notices, holding the
#                           pump: every stdin line behind it waits too.
#   in_pipe|waiting|stored -> queued
#                           in the tools row's in-memory Jobs.pending. A
#                           stored notice is marked notice-delivered BEFORE
#                           it is queued (deliverStoredNotices), on mount
#                           and by the 1 s file poll (loop.go and
#                           engine/notices.go pollStoredNotices).
#   queued -> delivered     a wake turn records it as its input, or the
#                           engine sends it to a turn already running (at
#                           the end of the request in flight, or on one of
#                           its own while a tool such as an ask runs).
#   -> lost                 see the findings below.
#
# proc is the parent's process: none (no process), starting (serve's lease
# reserved, stdin not there yet), live (serve's headless child), cli (the
# person resumed it in the TUI or `bough -r`; serve has no lease and
# appends to the file under the flock, so seqs never collide: the mapped
# model's "second writer" bug is refuted by history.AppendFile). gap is a
# live parent whose job-notices service is not mounted (the tools row
# reloading or failed): hlNotify answers false. ask is a pending tools.ask
# or secret inside the parent's turn. prompt is one line a person sends
# the parent while this is going on.
#
# Budgets keep the graph small: one kill, two starts, one reload, one
# resume in the CLI, one ask, one prompt.
#
# FINDINGS (the code as of main 5471918e; the invariants below are the
# ones the code keeps, the promises it breaks are the lost states, and
# LossOnlyThroughKnownWindows names every way in):
#   crash_after_key   Reported is saved before notifyFrom runs: serve dying
#                     between the two suppresses the report forever (the
#                     restart's re-report finds key <= Reported).
#   pipe              the stdin line is durable nowhere: the parent dies
#                     before its pump reads it.
#   killed_in_gap     the parent dies while hlNotice waits for job-notices.
#   gap_timeout       job-notices is not back within 30 s: hlNotice drops
#                     the notice (an error line, nothing stored).
#   killed_before_wake queued in memory (and, from a file, already marked
#                     delivered) when the parent dies: the wake turn that
#                     would have recorded it never runs.
#   secret_answer     a pending tools.secret takes the raw stdin line
#                     before hlLineIn sniffs {"notice"}: the notice JSON
#                     is taken as the secret's value (its store then fails
#                     on the JSON's characters) and the report is gone.
#                     (A plain ask is safe: the sniff runs first.)
#   stranded (fixed)  the engine's 1 s poll moved its size mark while
#                     job-notices was missing, so a notice appended during
#                     a tools-row reload waited for the file's next write.
#                     The server walk found the wait ended at random (an
#                     engine remount at the reload's end sometimes read the
#                     file again); pollStoredNotices now keeps its mark
#                     until job-notices is back, and Poll waits out the gap.
#   A person's prompt or steer line written behind a waiting notice waits
#   with it (up to 30 s) although hlSubmit itself does not need
#   job-notices; SIGINT interrupts are not stdin lines and are not held.

MAX_KILLS = 1
MAX_STARTS = 2
MAX_RELOADS = 1

SETTLED = ("delivered", "lost")
KNOWN_LOSSES = ("", "crash_after_key", "pipe", "killed_in_gap", "gap_timeout", "killed_before_wake", "secret_answer")

role Flow:
    action Init:
        self.report = "closed"
        self.proc = "none"
        self.busy = False
        self.gap = False
        self.ask = "none"
        self.prompt = "none"
        self.lost_how = ""
        self.delivered = 0
        # which pending ask, if any, took the notice line as its answer
        self.answered_by_notice = "none"
        self.starts = 0
        self.kills = 0
        self.reloads = 0
        self.resumed = False
        self.asked = False

    # ---- the report (serve) ----

    # system: report finds the closing entry and saves meta.Reported.
    atomic fair action Key:
        require self.report == "closed"
        self.report = "keyed"

    # system: serve dies (crash, kill -9) after saving Reported and before
    # notifyFrom; the restart's report finds the key already taken.
    atomic action ServeCrash:
        require self.report == "keyed"
        self.report = "lost"
        self.lost_how = "crash_after_key"

    # system: notifyFrom reads s.kids under the mutex, then drops it.
    atomic fair action Route:
        require self.report == "keyed"
        if self.proc in ("live", "starting"):
            self.report = "routed_stdin"
        else:
            self.report = "routed_file"

    # system: writeLine {notice}. Waits for a starting lease (started());
    # a child that died since the check fails the write and notifyFrom
    # falls through to AppendFile.
    atomic fair action WriteStdin:
        require self.report == "routed_stdin" and self.proc != "starting"
        if self.proc == "live":
            self.report = "in_pipe"
        else:
            self.report = "stored"

    # system: AppendFile notice (the parent may have started since Route).
    atomic fair action Append:
        require self.report == "routed_file"
        self.report = "stored"

    # ---- the parent's process ----

    # system: EnsureRecipient / Send / Adopt reserve a lease and spawn.
    atomic action Ensure:
        require self.proc == "none" and self.starts < MAX_STARTS
        self.proc = "starting"
        self.starts += 1

    # system: the child's loop mounts: deliverStoredNotices reads the
    # whole file once, marks and queues what is addressed to it.
    atomic fair action Mount:
        require self.proc == "starting"
        self.proc = "live"
        if self.report == "stored":
            self.report = "queued"

    # user: resumes the parent in the TUI (`bough -r`) with no serve lease.
    atomic action ResumeInCli:
        require self.proc == "none" and not self.resumed
        self.proc = "cli"
        self.resumed = True
        if self.report == "stored":
            self.report = "queued"

    # system: the parent's process dies (archive, Kill, crash, quit).
    # Memory goes with it: the pipe, a waiting hlNotice, Jobs.pending.
    atomic action Kill:
        require self.proc != "none" and self.kills < MAX_KILLS
        self.kills += 1
        self.proc = "none"
        self.busy = False
        self.gap = False
        self.ask = "none"
        if self.prompt == "behind":
            self.prompt = "sent"
        if self.report == "in_pipe":
            self.report = "lost"
            self.lost_how = "pipe"
        elif self.report == "waiting":
            self.report = "lost"
            self.lost_how = "killed_in_gap"
        elif self.report == "queued":
            self.report = "lost"
            self.lost_how = "killed_before_wake"

    # system: the tools row reloads (or fails): job-notices is gone.
    atomic action ReloadStart:
        require self.proc == "live" and not self.gap and self.reloads < MAX_RELOADS
        self.gap = True
        self.reloads += 1

    # system: job-notices is back; a waiting hlNotice's next retry queues
    # it and the pump moves on to the line behind it
    # (inlined: fizz applied only a role func's first assignment).
    atomic fair action ReloadEnd:
        require self.gap
        self.gap = False
        if self.report == "waiting":
            self.report = "queued"
            if self.prompt == "behind":
                self.prompt = "sent"
                self.busy = True

    # system: hlNoticeWait (30 s) runs out first: dropped, pump released.
    atomic fair action NoticeTimeout:
        require self.report == "waiting"
        self.report = "lost"
        self.lost_how = "gap_timeout"
        if self.prompt == "behind":
            self.prompt = "sent"
            self.busy = True

    # ---- the parent's pump and loop ----

    # system: the headless pump reads the stdin line (hlLineIn).
    atomic fair action PumpReads:
        require self.report == "in_pipe" and self.proc == "live"
        if self.ask == "secret":
            # hlAnswerPending(line) runs before the {"notice"} sniff.
            self.answered_by_notice = self.ask
            self.ask = "none"
            self.report = "lost"
            self.lost_how = "secret_answer"
        elif self.gap:
            self.report = "waiting"
        else:
            self.report = "queued"

    # system: the 1 s poll sees the file grew. With job-notices missing it
    # keeps its mark and reads again once the service is back.
    atomic fair action Poll:
        require self.report == "stored" and self.proc in ("live", "cli") and not self.gap
        self.report = "queued"

    # system: an idle loop's wake runs a turn whose input is the notice.
    atomic fair action Wake:
        require self.report == "queued" and self.proc in ("live", "cli") and not self.busy and not self.gap
        self.report = "delivered"
        self.delivered += 1
        self.busy = True

    # system: the engine sends the notice to the running turn at the end
    # of the request in flight, or on a request of its own when none is:
    # tools run asynchronously, so a pending ask or secret does not hold
    # it back (the server walk found this; the ask == "none" this required
    # was the loop's landJobs, not the engine's).
    atomic fair action Land:
        require self.report == "queued" and self.busy
        self.report = "delivered"
        self.delivered += 1

    # system: the parent's turn ends (not while an ask blocks it).
    atomic fair action TurnEnds:
        require self.busy and self.ask == "none"
        self.busy = False

    # agent: tools.ask / tools.secret inside the parent's turn.
    atomic action Ask:
        require self.busy and self.ask == "none" and not self.asked
        self.ask = "ask"
        self.asked = True

    atomic action AskSecret:
        require self.busy and self.ask == "none" and not self.asked
        self.ask = "secret"
        self.asked = True

    # user: answers the pending ask.
    atomic fair action Answer:
        require self.ask != "none"
        self.ask = "none"

    # user: prompts the parent while the notice is on its way. On a live
    # child it is a stdin line: behind a waiting notice it waits too.
    atomic action Prompt:
        require self.proc in ("live", "cli") and self.prompt == "none" and self.ask == "none"
        if self.proc == "live" and self.report == "waiting":
            self.prompt = "behind"
        else:
            self.prompt = "sent"
            self.busy = True

action Init:
    flow = Flow()

# Never twice: no path hands the parent's model the same report again
# (mark-before-queue, Reported, and the no-fallthrough stdin write).
always assertion DeliveredAtMostOnce:
    return flow.delivered <= 1

# delivered is exactly the report's state saying so.
always assertion DeliveredMeansCounted:
    return (flow.report == "delivered") == (flow.delivered == 1)

# The weaker form of "exactly once" the code keeps: a report that does not
# reach the model was lost through one of the named windows above, never
# silently.
always assertion LossOnlyThroughKnownWindows:
    return flow.lost_how in KNOWN_LOSSES and ((flow.report == "lost") == (flow.lost_how != ""))

# A plain ask is never answered by a notice line: only a secret is (the
# finding secret_answer, which loses the report).
always assertion NoticeNeverAnswersPlainAsk:
    return flow.answered_by_notice != "ask"

# A person's line is held only behind a notice waiting for job-notices,
# and never while the parent's own services are up.
always assertion PromptHeldOnlyInGap:
    return flow.prompt != "behind" or (flow.report == "waiting" and flow.gap)

# Every report settles: delivered, lost through a named window,
# or parked durably in the file of a parent with no process,
# for its next mount.
always eventually assertion ReportSettles:
    return flow.report in SETTLED or (flow.report == "stored" and flow.proc == "none")

# A live, idle parent with its services up eventually runs a wake turn for
# a notice it holds.
always eventually assertion QueuedIsDelivered:
    return flow.report != "queued" or flow.proc == "none"
